  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#tables-2\r\n\r\n> colgroup\\[hidden\\], col\\[hidden\\], thead\\[hidden\\], tbody\\[hidden\\],\r\n> tfoot\\[hidden\\], tr\\[hidden\\], td\\[hidden\\], th\\[hidden\\] \\{\r\n>   visibility:​ collapse;\r\n> \\}\r\n\r\nVisibility:collapse doesn't do anything on TH and TD elements. I doubt the proposed behavior is web-compatible in that case. Is there a specific reason we believe [hidden] on a table-cell should set visibility to hidden rather than rearrange the cells in the row?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/11264",
